1
00:00:01,914 --> 00:00:02,915
[instrumental music]

2
00:00:04,308 --> 00:00:06,528
[Jane]
Oh, it's lovely.

3
00:00:06,615 --> 00:00:07,920
[Lisbon]
It's a crime scene.

4
00:00:08,008 --> 00:00:09,661
[Patrick]
It's a lovely crime scene.

5
00:00:09,748 --> 00:00:11,489
[Rigsby]
Hey, couple joggers
found our John Doe

6
00:00:11,576 --> 00:00:12,534
on their morning run.

7
00:00:12,621 --> 00:00:13,839
Body's still pretty fresh.

8
00:00:13,926 --> 00:00:15,189
It must have happened
last night.

9
00:00:15,276 --> 00:00:17,365
No signs of an entry
or exit wound.

10
00:00:17,452 --> 00:00:19,410
It means cause was probably a
blunt force trauma to the head.

11
00:00:19,497 --> 00:00:21,064
And they brought
in the grown-ups

12
00:00:21,151 --> 00:00:22,805
because they couldn't
decide whose sandbox it was?

13
00:00:22,892 --> 00:00:24,546
Right, body's right
on the city line.

14
00:00:24,633 --> 00:00:26,069
'The only thing
they canagree on'

15
00:00:26,156 --> 00:00:28,028
'is that it was a carjacking
gone wrong.'

16
00:00:28,115 --> 00:00:29,899
Wallet, watch, wedding band,
everything gone.

17
00:00:32,162 --> 00:00:34,121
Oh, not everything.

18
00:00:34,208 --> 00:00:35,774
Killer would have been
very frustrated

19
00:00:35,861 --> 00:00:37,167
'to not be able to take this.'

20
00:00:37,254 --> 00:00:38,690
It looks like a wheel.

21
00:00:38,777 --> 00:00:40,214
Motorcycle wheel.

22
00:00:40,301 --> 00:00:42,129
I don't buy it as a carjacking.

23
00:00:42,216 --> 00:00:44,087
'Maybe the murderer
was covering it up as one'

24
00:00:44,174 --> 00:00:46,350
but if you're after someone's
car and valuables

25
00:00:46,437 --> 00:00:47,743
you grab and bolt.

26
00:00:47,830 --> 00:00:49,397
'You don't waste time
taking off a cufflink.'

27
00:00:49,484 --> 00:00:51,964
Right, carjacking,
a gunshot or a stab wound

28
00:00:52,052 --> 00:00:53,183
is more likely than a beating.

29
00:00:53,270 --> 00:00:54,967
Beating like this
takes time.

30
00:00:55,055 --> 00:00:56,230
The murder was personal.

31
00:00:56,317 --> 00:00:57,448
No surprise there.

32
00:00:57,535 --> 00:00:58,971
The haircut,
the suit, the cologne.

33
00:00:59,059 --> 00:01:00,321
This man had enemies.

34
00:01:00,408 --> 00:01:01,757
His cologne tells you
he had enemies?

35
00:01:01,844 --> 00:01:04,803
Sure.
Okay, confrontational.

36
00:01:04,890 --> 00:01:06,936
Finishing touch
on a wardrobe that says

37
00:01:07,023 --> 00:01:09,591
"Pay attention.
Show respect."

38
00:01:09,678 --> 00:01:11,984
This was an extrovert,
tough guy, a professional.

39
00:01:12,072 --> 00:01:14,683
A backroom politician
or a lawyer, a fixer.

40
00:01:14,770 --> 00:01:16,511
'The type that's good
with people.'

41
00:01:16,598 --> 00:01:19,688
Makin' people do things
they maybe don't wanna do.

42
00:01:19,775 --> 00:01:22,343
Uh, what he is, is useless
until we know whohe is.

43
00:01:23,866 --> 00:01:25,128
Well, I can do that too.

44
00:01:27,478 --> 00:01:29,524
Oh, no, Jane. I, uh, I checked.
The phone's not on him--

45
00:01:29,611 --> 00:01:31,395
The signal light's still on.
Phone's in range.

46
00:01:31,482 --> 00:01:33,354
His assailant probably
threw it in the trees.

47
00:01:35,530 --> 00:01:36,792
What are you doing?

48
00:01:36,879 --> 00:01:38,228
I'm makin' a call.

49
00:01:38,315 --> 00:01:39,795
But you don't have
the phone.

50
00:01:39,882 --> 00:01:41,971
- I have my voice.
- You still need the phone.

51
00:01:42,058 --> 00:01:44,408
Wanna use the voice activation?
You need its names and numbers.

52
00:01:44,495 --> 00:01:46,802
There is one name
programmed into every phone

53
00:01:46,889 --> 00:01:49,500
particularly into one
belonging to a middle-aged man

54
00:01:49,587 --> 00:01:50,980
that was wearing
a wedding band.

55
00:01:52,808 --> 00:01:53,939
Home.

56
00:01:56,072 --> 00:01:57,856
[phone ringing]

57
00:02:00,381 --> 00:02:01,512
[female #1]
'Hello?'

58
00:02:01,599 --> 00:02:03,297
Hello,
this is Patrick Jane

59
00:02:03,384 --> 00:02:04,863
from the California Bureau
of Investigation.

60
00:02:04,950 --> 00:02:07,823
I was wondering if you knew
a man six feet tall, mid 40s

61
00:02:07,910 --> 00:02:11,174
salt and pepper hair,
gray custom-made suit

62
00:02:11,261 --> 00:02:14,003
weighing about 192,
give or take?

63
00:02:14,090 --> 00:02:15,700
[female #1]
'That's my husband
Gordon Hodge.'

64
00:02:15,787 --> 00:02:18,703
- Gordon Hodge?
- 'You said you're from CBI?'

65
00:02:18,790 --> 00:02:20,270
'Is something wrong?'

66
00:02:20,357 --> 00:02:22,054
Uh, just a sec.

67
00:02:22,142 --> 00:02:23,360
It's for you.

68
00:02:30,106 --> 00:02:31,151
Hello?

69
00:02:32,195 --> 00:02:34,589
[theme music]

70
00:02:43,337 --> 00:02:45,730
[instrumental music]

71
00:03:00,832 --> 00:03:03,139
[doorbell ringing]

72
00:03:03,226 --> 00:03:06,229
[Mrs. Hodge]
I knew that something like this
would happen sooner or later.

73
00:03:06,316 --> 00:03:09,928
[Lisbon]
Well, was your husband having
some sort of trouble lately?

74
00:03:10,015 --> 00:03:13,976
Gordon was a criminal attorney
with a very special practice.

75
00:03:14,063 --> 00:03:17,849
He had only one client,
the Sinner Saints.

76
00:03:17,936 --> 00:03:19,677
- Bikers, are they?
- Yeah.

77
00:03:19,764 --> 00:03:22,332
They're one of the top
biker gangs in the state.

78
00:03:22,419 --> 00:03:24,160
They run some legit businesses,
but mostly

79
00:03:24,247 --> 00:03:26,423
they're into drugs
and prostitution

80
00:03:26,510 --> 00:03:29,948
'low-rent protection rackets,
that kind of thing.'

81
00:03:30,035 --> 00:03:31,820
[Mrs. Hodge]
'For years, I begged
him to get out'

82
00:03:31,907 --> 00:03:34,257
'but Gordon said that'

83
00:03:34,344 --> 00:03:36,564
'a lawyer never abandons
his client.'

84
00:03:36,651 --> 00:03:39,044
It's unethical.

85
00:03:39,131 --> 00:03:40,263
It's what he always
called them.

86
00:03:40,350 --> 00:03:43,484
Never the gang,
always the client.

87
00:03:43,571 --> 00:03:45,921
When was the last time
you saw him?

88
00:03:46,008 --> 00:03:48,663
[Mrs. Hodge]
'Yesterday morning,
before work.'

89
00:03:48,750 --> 00:03:50,665
Gordon used to meet
these people at all hours.

90
00:03:50,752 --> 00:03:51,796
That's how they are.

91
00:03:51,883 --> 00:03:53,624
So, we didn't get worried

92
00:03:53,711 --> 00:03:55,887
'when he didn't come home
last night.'

93
00:03:55,974 --> 00:03:57,846
Had he been acting
differently lately?

94
00:03:57,933 --> 00:04:00,762
He'd been more on edge
the last week or so.

95
00:04:00,849 --> 00:04:03,155
I think something happened
at work, but I'm not sure what.

96
00:04:04,548 --> 00:04:05,854
Did you ask him
about it?

97
00:04:05,941 --> 00:04:09,727
No, never.
Work was off limits.

98
00:04:12,252 --> 00:04:13,644
He said it was boring.

99
00:04:13,731 --> 00:04:14,819
What was the real reason?

100
00:04:16,821 --> 00:04:18,997
Do you think he was ashamed,
or he sensed your shame?

101
00:04:20,782 --> 00:04:22,087
He wanted to protect us.

102
00:04:25,047 --> 00:04:26,831
Would his colleagues
at the office

103
00:04:26,918 --> 00:04:28,093
have known
what was going on?

104
00:04:28,180 --> 00:04:29,530
No, he was a one-man shop.

105
00:04:29,617 --> 00:04:31,662
Didn't even have a secretary.

106
00:04:31,749 --> 00:04:35,057
'Gordon didn't trust anyone
with his business.'

107
00:04:35,144 --> 00:04:37,886
[Lisbon]
'Any idea who might
have wanted to kill him?'

108
00:04:37,973 --> 00:04:40,802
Well, you might wanna
ask his client.

109
00:04:40,889 --> 00:04:43,195
He knew all their secrets.

110
00:04:43,283 --> 00:04:45,546
He probably learned something
that he shouldn't have.

111
00:04:45,633 --> 00:04:48,418
Either of you ever meet
any of those scumbags?

112
00:04:48,505 --> 00:04:49,593
No.

113
00:04:50,986 --> 00:04:52,727
You two must be very torn.

114
00:04:52,814 --> 00:04:54,555
Living in such a beautiful home.

115
00:04:54,642 --> 00:04:57,297
'Driving nice cars,
going to good schools.'

116
00:04:57,384 --> 00:04:59,211
All paid for
by dangerous criminals

117
00:04:59,299 --> 00:05:03,607
or, uh, scumbags,
as my colleague says.

118
00:05:03,694 --> 00:05:07,394
Do I wish that Gordon would have
defended civil rights leaders?

119
00:05:07,481 --> 00:05:09,221
Yes, of course!

120
00:05:09,309 --> 00:05:11,746
'But he believed that everyone
had a constitutional right'

121
00:05:11,833 --> 00:05:15,271
to have a good defense.
He had his principles.

122
00:05:19,754 --> 00:05:21,146
Thank you for your time.

123
00:05:26,151 --> 00:05:28,458
Did you go to some interview
school I've never heard of?

124
00:05:28,545 --> 00:05:30,504
Next time, get the facts,
save the editorial.

125
00:05:30,591 --> 00:05:32,419
Yes, ma'am.

126
00:05:32,506 --> 00:05:34,812
I know,Jane did it too.
He's not a CBI agent.

127
00:05:34,899 --> 00:05:36,640
From you, I expect
professional standards.

128
00:05:36,727 --> 00:05:38,076
Yes, boss.

129
00:05:38,163 --> 00:05:39,513
That was the captain
of the local CHIPS.

130
00:05:39,600 --> 00:05:40,992
Hodge's car was just
fished out of a lake

131
00:05:41,079 --> 00:05:42,342
about a mile
from the murder scene.

132
00:05:42,429 --> 00:05:43,517
No good for prints.

133
00:05:43,604 --> 00:05:44,822
'He said that two weeks back'

134
00:05:44,909 --> 00:05:46,563
'they busted Hodge
at a highway rest stop'

135
00:05:46,650 --> 00:05:48,304
walkin' to his car
with two ounces of coke

136
00:05:48,391 --> 00:05:49,958
and two ounces
of meth in his pockets.

137
00:05:50,045 --> 00:05:51,133
Nailed him
with felony possession.

138
00:05:51,220 --> 00:05:52,264
Nice.

139
00:05:52,352 --> 00:05:54,310
Only the DA dropped the charges.

140
00:05:54,397 --> 00:05:56,007
'There was some
unlawful search technicality.'

141
00:05:56,094 --> 00:05:57,618
[Lisbon]
'Either Hodge
is a great lawyer..'

142
00:05:57,705 --> 00:05:59,141
Or the DA turned him
in exchange for dropping

143
00:05:59,228 --> 00:06:01,317
the charges, planned to
use him as an informant.

144
00:06:01,404 --> 00:06:03,232
- Well if the Saints found out--
- Yeah, they'd kill him.

145
00:06:03,319 --> 00:06:04,581
They didknow about the charges.

146
00:06:04,668 --> 00:06:06,322
Their boss, Von McBride,
posted Hodge's bail.

147
00:06:06,409 --> 00:06:07,584
[Lisbon]
'Well, talk to your friends
at the DA.'

148
00:06:07,671 --> 00:06:09,151
Find out what
the story is there.

149
00:06:09,238 --> 00:06:10,892
Jane and I'll go talk
to the Sinner Saints.

150
00:06:10,979 --> 00:06:12,894
- Okay, be careful.
- Want me to come for backup?

151
00:06:12,981 --> 00:06:15,984
Uh, no. Talk to forensics
about the car.

152
00:06:16,071 --> 00:06:18,029
Jane, let's go.

153
00:06:18,116 --> 00:06:19,596
Now, please?

154
00:06:19,683 --> 00:06:20,815
Come on.

155
00:06:25,297 --> 00:06:27,778
[instrumental music]

156
00:06:40,225 --> 00:06:42,619
[music continues]

157
00:06:47,798 --> 00:06:50,235
- Beautiful, huh?
- No, not really.

158
00:06:50,322 --> 00:06:51,759
I fail to see the charm.

159
00:06:51,846 --> 00:06:53,500
It's the glamour
of mobility.

160
00:06:53,587 --> 00:06:55,589
That's why the girls
went for Cain, and not Abel.

161
00:06:55,676 --> 00:06:57,808
- Is that right?
- Yeah, nomads.

162
00:06:57,895 --> 00:06:59,375
Sexier than farmers.

163
00:06:59,462 --> 00:07:01,116
They have romance.

164
00:07:01,203 --> 00:07:03,597
[cell phone ringing]

165
00:07:04,336 --> 00:07:05,729
Lisbon.

166
00:07:05,816 --> 00:07:07,035
I spoke to my friend
in the DA's office.

167
00:07:07,122 --> 00:07:08,689
They didn't make
a deal with Hodge.

168
00:07:08,776 --> 00:07:10,517
'They let him go because
the case was less than ironclad'

169
00:07:10,604 --> 00:07:12,606
and they've already lost too
many to Hodge and the Saints.

170
00:07:12,693 --> 00:07:14,869
Last ten years, they've beaten
the rap in over 50 cases.

171
00:07:14,956 --> 00:07:17,306
Murder, rape, drug trafficking.
They're bulletproof.

172
00:07:17,393 --> 00:07:19,221
Nobody's bulletproof.

173
00:07:19,308 --> 00:07:22,137
Well, the DA says
to stay away from them.

174
00:07:22,224 --> 00:07:23,443
'They're bad news.'

175
00:07:23,530 --> 00:07:25,357
Good, sound lawyerly advice.

176
00:07:25,445 --> 00:07:27,316
I'll take that
under advisement.

177
00:07:29,405 --> 00:07:30,798
- You ready?
- Whoo.

178
00:07:34,236 --> 00:07:37,021
[heavy metal music]

179
00:07:42,462 --> 00:07:44,202
There's romance for you.

180
00:07:47,684 --> 00:07:49,077
We're with the CBI.

181
00:07:49,164 --> 00:07:51,688
We're looking
for Von McBride.

182
00:07:51,775 --> 00:07:54,648
Not here, which is where
you need to be.

183
00:07:54,735 --> 00:07:56,606
Well, can you tell us
where he is?

184
00:07:58,390 --> 00:07:59,696
No, I cannot.

185
00:08:02,525 --> 00:08:04,571
[Lisbon]
Listen, we're here
for information.

186
00:08:04,658 --> 00:08:06,224
'Not trouble, guys.'

187
00:08:06,311 --> 00:08:09,576
[male #1]
'Well, we've got nothing
to say.'

188
00:08:09,663 --> 00:08:11,273
[Lisbon]
'I can take you in
if you want me to.'

189
00:08:11,360 --> 00:08:12,709
'I prefer to talk here.'

190
00:08:12,796 --> 00:08:14,015
[male #1]
'Like I said'

191
00:08:14,102 --> 00:08:15,843
'we've got nothin'
to talk about.'

192
00:08:15,930 --> 00:08:17,584
'We're not doing
anythin' illegal.'

193
00:08:17,671 --> 00:08:19,455
Mr. McBride?

194
00:08:19,542 --> 00:08:21,631
Your focus
on this pressing matter

195
00:08:21,718 --> 00:08:23,415
suggests you're the man
in charge here.

196
00:08:23,503 --> 00:08:25,983
Yeah, well,
keep on walking, blondie.

197
00:08:26,070 --> 00:08:28,464
We just have a few questions
for you. It won't take long.

198
00:08:28,551 --> 00:08:31,989
Yeah, well, I'm sorry, I don't,
uh, talk to police officers

199
00:08:32,076 --> 00:08:33,513
on the advice of my lawyer.

200
00:08:34,818 --> 00:08:36,298
Your lawyer's dead.

201
00:08:36,385 --> 00:08:37,952
Yeah, I heard that.

202
00:08:38,039 --> 00:08:40,171
But his advice is still good.

203
00:08:40,258 --> 00:08:42,739
Means your business here
is done.

204
00:08:42,826 --> 00:08:45,525
Oh, you don't wanna know
who the informant is then?

205
00:08:47,135 --> 00:08:48,353
What informant?

206
00:08:48,440 --> 00:08:49,616
Oh, I'm sorry.
Forget I spoke.

207
00:08:49,703 --> 00:08:51,661
I'm so sorry.

208
00:08:51,748 --> 00:08:52,923
You messin' with me?

209
00:08:53,010 --> 00:08:53,968
Yeah, I'm messing with you.

210
00:08:54,055 --> 00:08:55,230
There's no informant.

211
00:08:56,797 --> 00:08:58,886
Come here.

212
00:08:58,973 --> 00:09:00,365
You touch him,
and I'll arrest you.

213
00:09:02,193 --> 00:09:04,369
I would loveto see you
try and do that.

214
00:09:04,456 --> 00:09:06,502
What's your name?

215
00:09:06,589 --> 00:09:08,809
- Xander.
- Xander.

216
00:09:08,896 --> 00:09:11,551
Your threats are empty.
She's a state agent.

217
00:09:11,638 --> 00:09:12,943
You're not gonna lay
a finger on her

218
00:09:13,030 --> 00:09:15,206
'and you know that,
so why play tough?'

219
00:09:15,293 --> 00:09:18,296
W-where's that come from?
This need to intimidate?

220
00:09:18,383 --> 00:09:20,690
I'm a sadist,
and I bore easily.

221
00:09:20,777 --> 00:09:23,954
Oh, me, I see
a difficult childhood.

222
00:09:24,041 --> 00:09:26,261
Bad parenting,
a lot of torment.

223
00:09:26,348 --> 00:09:29,873
But I also see how
that suffering gave you

224
00:09:29,960 --> 00:09:31,788
great powers of empathy
and a strong creative side.

225
00:09:31,875 --> 00:09:33,181
And those are the qualities

226
00:09:33,268 --> 00:09:35,052
you should try
and nurture in yourself.

227
00:09:35,139 --> 00:09:37,489
Not this brutish character
you try to hide behind.

228
00:09:39,579 --> 00:09:40,928
Oh, that's Xander, alright.

229
00:09:42,930 --> 00:09:44,061
Full of empathy.

230
00:09:48,065 --> 00:09:49,153
You guys want a drink?

231
00:09:50,677 --> 00:09:52,504
Sure.

232
00:09:52,592 --> 00:09:55,682
So what's this crap
about an informant?

233
00:09:55,769 --> 00:09:58,336
How long have you known about
Hodge's taste for coke and meth?

234
00:09:59,816 --> 00:10:01,383
Couple of years.

235
00:10:01,470 --> 00:10:04,865
Guy liked to party,
but he could still do his job.

236
00:10:04,952 --> 00:10:07,998
[Jane]
Couldn't have been too thrilled
when he got busted.

237
00:10:08,085 --> 00:10:09,434
Case got dropped.

238
00:10:09,521 --> 00:10:11,872
Must have wondered why.

239
00:10:11,959 --> 00:10:13,308
Illegal search.

240
00:10:13,395 --> 00:10:14,875
Yeah.

241
00:10:14,962 --> 00:10:18,269
Either that or Hodge,
uh, flipped on you.

242
00:10:18,356 --> 00:10:20,315
- That son of a--
- Hold on a second, Diamond.

243
00:10:20,402 --> 00:10:21,533
He didn't flip.

244
00:10:22,796 --> 00:10:23,971
There is no informant.

245
00:10:25,581 --> 00:10:26,626
Where were you last night?

246
00:10:26,713 --> 00:10:28,584
Right here.

247
00:10:28,671 --> 00:10:29,977
And I got 30 other brothers

248
00:10:30,064 --> 00:10:31,413
who will vouch for me
and each other.

249
00:10:31,500 --> 00:10:35,591
Look, man,
none of my guys did this.

250
00:10:35,678 --> 00:10:38,594
We loved Gordon, man. He was
like a member of the club.

251
00:10:38,681 --> 00:10:40,248
Yeah, he couldn't ride
worth a damn.

252
00:10:40,335 --> 00:10:41,597
No, he couldn't, huh?

253
00:10:41,684 --> 00:10:43,817
He tried though.

254
00:10:43,904 --> 00:10:45,166
Then, who killed him?

255
00:10:45,253 --> 00:10:46,776
[McBride]
'My guess?'

256
00:10:46,863 --> 00:10:48,517
Probably some other
motorcycle club

257
00:10:48,604 --> 00:10:50,867
looking to put us
out of business.

258
00:10:50,954 --> 00:10:52,042
Chaos Brigade.

259
00:10:54,349 --> 00:10:55,655
Bolos Plata.

260
00:10:55,742 --> 00:10:57,657
[female #2]
'Get your hands
off of me.'

261
00:10:57,744 --> 00:10:59,659
'Get off me.'

262
00:10:59,746 --> 00:11:02,923
Help! Get your hands
off of me.

263
00:11:03,010 --> 00:11:04,968
Get off of me.

264
00:11:05,055 --> 00:11:06,143
Get off of me.

265
00:11:06,230 --> 00:11:07,928
Let her go,
and back away!

266
00:11:08,015 --> 00:11:10,017
- Back away now!
- Get your hands off me.

267
00:11:12,497 --> 00:11:14,151
You're murderers.

268
00:11:14,238 --> 00:11:15,805
All of you.

269
00:11:15,892 --> 00:11:18,199
Ma'am, take it easy.
I'm CBI.

270
00:11:18,286 --> 00:11:19,243
Ma'am!

271
00:11:19,330 --> 00:11:20,984
Police. Stop!

272
00:11:21,071 --> 00:11:22,420
Out of the way.
Ma'am!

273
00:11:23,378 --> 00:11:25,772
[dramatic music]

274
00:11:30,907 --> 00:11:33,344
Who was that?
Is she a friend of yours?

275
00:11:33,431 --> 00:11:35,477
Never seen her before.

276
00:11:35,564 --> 00:11:38,654
Mentally deranged,
seems like. Poor thing.

277
00:11:38,741 --> 00:11:41,265
You know,
you're a very good liar.

278
00:11:41,352 --> 00:11:43,572
Most people subconsciously
signal dishonesty

279
00:11:43,659 --> 00:11:46,053
but you, there's nothing.
No inner conflict.

280
00:11:46,140 --> 00:11:47,358
Usually, that's the mark

281
00:11:47,445 --> 00:11:50,797
of what shrinks
like to call a sociopath.

282
00:11:50,884 --> 00:11:53,582
Well, if by sociopath,
you mean that if you cross me

283
00:11:53,669 --> 00:11:56,498
I would enjoy watching you
suffer pain before I kill you..

284
00:11:58,500 --> 00:12:00,197
...then, yeah,
I'm a sociopath.

285
00:12:01,721 --> 00:12:02,852
See ya.

286
00:12:05,507 --> 00:12:06,682
Bye.

287
00:12:15,909 --> 00:12:17,562
[Rigsby]
So, we talked
to the gang unit.

288
00:12:17,649 --> 00:12:19,739
There's no other biker gang
that would cross the Saints

289
00:12:19,826 --> 00:12:21,784
and run the risk of starting
a war that they couldn't win.

290
00:12:21,871 --> 00:12:23,525
[Jane]
This is incredible.
You should see this.

291
00:12:23,612 --> 00:12:25,440
Hold on. Anything on
the woman in the parking lot?

292
00:12:25,527 --> 00:12:27,181
Sinner Saints
have their own website.

293
00:12:27,268 --> 00:12:29,226
- Really?
- Yeah.

294
00:12:29,313 --> 00:12:31,272
We cross-checked registrations
of the truck model and color

295
00:12:31,359 --> 00:12:33,100
with driver's license photos
fitting her description.

296
00:12:33,187 --> 00:12:35,319
No hits, truck must be
registered to her husband

297
00:12:35,406 --> 00:12:36,538
or other family member.

298
00:12:36,625 --> 00:12:37,887
McBride's clamming up about her

299
00:12:37,974 --> 00:12:38,932
means he's hiding something.

300
00:12:39,019 --> 00:12:40,194
He's merged two other gangs

301
00:12:40,281 --> 00:12:41,761
into the Saints
in the last five years.

302
00:12:41,848 --> 00:12:43,937
It's the fastest growing gang
in the nation.

303
00:12:44,024 --> 00:12:45,634
Go to Hodge's office,
see if you can find

304
00:12:45,721 --> 00:12:47,723
anything on the gang's
operation that pops.

305
00:12:47,810 --> 00:12:49,725
And have the Deerfield PD
issue a BOLO

306
00:12:49,812 --> 00:12:51,205
on the woman's pickup truck.

307
00:12:51,292 --> 00:12:53,250
- Right.
- You can buy logo merchandise.

308
00:12:53,337 --> 00:12:57,341
Sinner Saints coffee mugs,
decals, beach towels. Whoa!

309
00:12:57,428 --> 00:13:00,170
And some various other
interesting little knick-knacks.

310
00:13:00,257 --> 00:13:01,998
- Nice.
- Yeah.

311
00:13:02,085 --> 00:13:03,478
Well, if they do it,
we should do it.

312
00:13:03,565 --> 00:13:06,002
A range of casual wear, maybe?

313
00:13:06,089 --> 00:13:07,308
Sensible shoes?

314
00:13:09,266 --> 00:13:10,746
I'll get right on that.

315
00:13:12,356 --> 00:13:14,097
Lisbon loafers.

316
00:13:14,184 --> 00:13:15,316
Found something, boss.

317
00:13:16,883 --> 00:13:18,623
These are Gordon Hodge's
cell phone calls

318
00:13:18,710 --> 00:13:20,103
from the night
of the murder.

319
00:13:20,190 --> 00:13:21,844
All were routine business calls

320
00:13:21,931 --> 00:13:24,499
Von McBride, other lawyers,
court officials.

321
00:13:24,586 --> 00:13:27,676
'But it's the last call
that bumps.'

322
00:13:27,763 --> 00:13:30,592
"7:23, incoming
from a Constance Hoyt.

323
00:13:30,679 --> 00:13:31,898
Current address unknown."

324
00:13:31,985 --> 00:13:33,464
Must not want people
finding her.

325
00:13:33,551 --> 00:13:34,814
Well, I went back
three months.

326
00:13:34,901 --> 00:13:36,859
A lot of calls
between her and Hodge.

327
00:13:36,946 --> 00:13:38,469
- Did you try the number?
- Twice.

328
00:13:38,556 --> 00:13:40,558
Got one of those
computer voicemail messages.

329
00:13:40,645 --> 00:13:42,212
Plus, I ran her name
through the DMV

330
00:13:42,299 --> 00:13:43,823
for registration
of a black pickup truck.

331
00:13:43,910 --> 00:13:45,215
She's not
your parking lot woman.

332
00:13:45,302 --> 00:13:47,130
Check Von McBride's
cell phone records.

333
00:13:47,217 --> 00:13:49,829
See if he had any contact
with this Constance Hoyt.

334
00:13:53,876 --> 00:13:56,400
Bingo.
Couple of chatty Cathys.

335
00:13:56,487 --> 00:13:58,620
Talking three
or four times a day.

336
00:13:58,707 --> 00:13:59,708
Either she's his mom, or..

337
00:13:59,795 --> 00:14:01,057
His girlfriend.

338
00:14:04,104 --> 00:14:06,497
[heavy metal music]

339
00:14:18,988 --> 00:14:21,425
Constance?

340
00:14:21,512 --> 00:14:23,558
We just have a couple
questions for you.

341
00:14:23,645 --> 00:14:24,994
[motorcycle whirring]

342
00:14:25,081 --> 00:14:27,344
Constance.

343
00:14:27,431 --> 00:14:28,824
- I'll drive.
- No time!

344
00:14:28,911 --> 00:14:30,478
[dramatic music]

345
00:14:31,958 --> 00:14:33,263
- Boss, seat belt.
- Go!

346
00:14:36,092 --> 00:14:38,486
[music continues]

347
00:14:44,753 --> 00:14:45,841
[tires screeching]

348
00:14:49,671 --> 00:14:51,934
[music continues]

349
00:14:59,072 --> 00:15:00,725
Bike's got too much muscle.
You're gonna have to..

350
00:15:03,728 --> 00:15:06,122
[music continues]

351
00:15:30,016 --> 00:15:31,321
[grunting]

352
00:15:32,975 --> 00:15:34,585
[Van Pelt]
'Don't move.'

353
00:15:34,672 --> 00:15:35,978
[Lisbon]
'Keep your hands
where I can see 'em.'

354
00:15:36,065 --> 00:15:39,068
Do not even think
of moving.

355
00:15:39,155 --> 00:15:40,504
I gotta get you
out of the office more.

356
00:15:44,334 --> 00:15:45,379
You're under arrest.

357
00:15:50,688 --> 00:15:51,820
You got Hodge's office key?

358
00:15:53,300 --> 00:15:55,171
So what's your problem
with bikers?

359
00:15:55,258 --> 00:15:57,957
- I hate bikers.
- Why's that?

360
00:15:58,044 --> 00:16:00,394
- My dad was a biker.
- Really?

361
00:16:00,481 --> 00:16:02,613
I didn't know that.

362
00:16:02,700 --> 00:16:05,442
No? Well, I thought
you read my file.

363
00:16:05,529 --> 00:16:06,748
Well, it says
he was a big-time criminal.

364
00:16:06,835 --> 00:16:08,184
Didn't specify
any affiliations.

365
00:16:11,492 --> 00:16:13,581
Jimmy marks on the doorknob.

366
00:16:13,668 --> 00:16:15,496
I doubt that was part
of the original decor.

367
00:16:15,583 --> 00:16:17,977
[dramatic music]

368
00:16:27,334 --> 00:16:28,726
- Door's clear.
- Clear.

369
00:16:30,250 --> 00:16:31,294
The desk's clear.

370
00:16:35,385 --> 00:16:36,647
[sighs]

371
00:16:38,475 --> 00:16:40,260
Cracks are on the outside
of the window.

372
00:16:40,347 --> 00:16:42,001
It means a previous
break-in attempt.

373
00:16:42,088 --> 00:16:43,263
'I think they were looking
for something'

374
00:16:43,350 --> 00:16:44,742
or just trying
to send a message?

375
00:16:47,049 --> 00:16:48,398
Message was definitely
a part of it.

376
00:16:56,580 --> 00:16:58,713
Do you prefer Constance,
or Diamond?

377
00:17:00,280 --> 00:17:02,586
I prefer to get
the hell out of here.

378
00:17:02,673 --> 00:17:03,892
You ran from the police.

379
00:17:03,979 --> 00:17:06,025
Endangered the lives
of two agents.

380
00:17:06,112 --> 00:17:07,809
You could be here
a couple of days.

381
00:17:07,896 --> 00:17:10,072
- I don't think that's right.
- Why did you run?

382
00:17:10,159 --> 00:17:13,293
I ran because I'm deadif
anyone sees me talking to cops.

383
00:17:13,380 --> 00:17:15,425
The Saints are all paranoid
about informants now

384
00:17:15,512 --> 00:17:16,992
which is why
I'm not saying a word.

385
00:17:17,079 --> 00:17:19,081
Tell us about your affair
with Gordon Hodge.

386
00:17:22,128 --> 00:17:23,607
[scoffs]

387
00:17:23,694 --> 00:17:25,131
I wasn't sleeping with Gordon.

388
00:17:27,394 --> 00:17:28,569
Oh!

389
00:17:32,747 --> 00:17:35,010
Uh, yes, you were.

390
00:17:42,887 --> 00:17:45,238
It was only a few months.
We were just having fun.

391
00:17:45,325 --> 00:17:47,588
It's not like Von doesn't
sleep around on me and..

392
00:17:49,198 --> 00:17:50,504
Gordon treated me nice.

393
00:17:50,591 --> 00:17:52,201
You had genuine feelings
for him.

394
00:17:52,288 --> 00:17:54,203
He was decent.

395
00:17:54,290 --> 00:17:55,552
He never looked down
on you.

396
00:17:57,641 --> 00:18:00,122
He just got sucked in
too deep with the Saints.

397
00:18:00,209 --> 00:18:02,864
Did you know
he was arrested for possession?

398
00:18:02,951 --> 00:18:05,345
Told him a hundred times
to be careful..

399
00:18:05,432 --> 00:18:07,129
...but he got dumb
about it.

400
00:18:07,216 --> 00:18:09,653
Ah, well, drugs simply
make people careless.

401
00:18:09,740 --> 00:18:12,439
You had to be a little concerned
about McBride finding out.

402
00:18:12,526 --> 00:18:14,528
It would have made things
complicated.

403
00:18:14,615 --> 00:18:16,704
Complicated is one way
to put it.

404
00:18:16,791 --> 00:18:19,315
So you called him that night.
Then what happened?

405
00:18:19,402 --> 00:18:22,144
- Did you go and see him?
- No!

406
00:18:22,231 --> 00:18:24,190
No.

407
00:18:24,277 --> 00:18:26,714
I called to break it off.
I heard him answer the phone.

408
00:18:26,801 --> 00:18:30,848
And I'd tried to talk to him,
but the line went dead.

409
00:18:30,935 --> 00:18:32,372
What about the woman
in the parking lot?

410
00:18:32,459 --> 00:18:33,764
I don't know.

411
00:18:33,851 --> 00:18:35,418
Von doesn't talk
gang business with me.

412
00:18:35,505 --> 00:18:36,941
Had you seen her before?

413
00:18:37,028 --> 00:18:38,813
She's come around
a few times

414
00:18:38,900 --> 00:18:40,380
the last couple of weeks,
same thing.

415
00:18:40,467 --> 00:18:42,947
Lots of crazy yelling,
then taking off.

416
00:18:43,034 --> 00:18:44,166
Look..

417
00:18:45,124 --> 00:18:46,734
You, um..

418
00:18:46,821 --> 00:18:48,301
You gotta promise

419
00:18:48,388 --> 00:18:51,086
that Von doesn't find out
about me and Gordon.

420
00:18:51,173 --> 00:18:53,480
He keeps his cards close.

421
00:18:53,567 --> 00:18:55,177
He could already know.

422
00:18:55,264 --> 00:18:57,527
'Killed Hodge
out of jealousy.'

423
00:18:57,614 --> 00:18:59,703
Trust me.

424
00:18:59,790 --> 00:19:01,444
If Von knew..

425
00:19:01,531 --> 00:19:03,446
...Gordon's wouldn't be
the only dead body.

426
00:19:05,405 --> 00:19:06,841
Only one other person knew.

427
00:19:09,017 --> 00:19:10,627
And that was bad enough.

428
00:19:10,714 --> 00:19:12,020
Who was that other person?

429
00:19:15,545 --> 00:19:17,330
We have information
that suggests

430
00:19:17,417 --> 00:19:19,723
you knew about Gordon
and another woman.

431
00:19:22,857 --> 00:19:24,946
Yes, I did.

432
00:19:25,033 --> 00:19:27,427
How?

433
00:19:27,514 --> 00:19:30,560
About four months ago,
I found a valet stub

434
00:19:30,647 --> 00:19:33,868
on the driveway
from the Deerfield Inn.

435
00:19:33,955 --> 00:19:35,609
So one night,
I followed him

436
00:19:35,696 --> 00:19:39,090
and saw him go in
with that biker girl.

437
00:19:39,178 --> 00:19:41,354
Did you confront him?

438
00:19:41,441 --> 00:19:43,138
More like yell and hit him.

439
00:19:44,661 --> 00:19:46,794
He promised
he'd stop seeing her.

440
00:19:46,881 --> 00:19:48,187
I took him at his word

441
00:19:48,274 --> 00:19:50,319
and I never asked him
about it again.

442
00:19:50,406 --> 00:19:52,539
Why not?

443
00:19:52,626 --> 00:19:54,062
Because I didn't wanna
hear him lie to me.

444
00:19:55,672 --> 00:19:57,457
Mrs. Hodge..

445
00:19:57,544 --> 00:19:59,763
...if you picked up
on your husband's affair

446
00:19:59,850 --> 00:20:03,071
you must have suspected about
his other illicit activities.

447
00:20:03,158 --> 00:20:06,379
I knew about the drugs
and the partying.

448
00:20:06,466 --> 00:20:08,598
He was surrounded by it.

449
00:20:08,685 --> 00:20:10,948
Why didn't you tell us
about this earlier?

450
00:20:11,035 --> 00:20:12,820
Because Gordon is dead.

451
00:20:12,907 --> 00:20:15,736
Anything that I said or did
would not bring him back.

452
00:20:15,823 --> 00:20:19,043
My son draws stares
and whispers

453
00:20:19,130 --> 00:20:21,437
'because of his father,
Agent Lisbon.'

454
00:20:21,524 --> 00:20:24,527
Both of us,
we deserve to grieve

455
00:20:24,614 --> 00:20:26,790
without shame and scandal,
don't we?

456
00:20:28,052 --> 00:20:29,967
Yes, you do.

457
00:20:30,054 --> 00:20:31,839
And if she'd followed
her husband once before

458
00:20:31,926 --> 00:20:33,536
she could have tailed him again
and killed him.

459
00:20:33,623 --> 00:20:35,538
No, she didn't do it.
She loved him.

460
00:20:35,625 --> 00:20:37,671
She was a prisoner
of her husband's life.

461
00:20:37,758 --> 00:20:39,673
She gets rid of him,
gets a fresh start.

462
00:20:39,760 --> 00:20:41,718
People trapped
in miserable lives

463
00:20:41,805 --> 00:20:42,850
always talk about escaping.

464
00:20:42,937 --> 00:20:44,330
Few actually do it.

465
00:20:44,417 --> 00:20:45,853
It's easier just
to close your eyes

466
00:20:45,940 --> 00:20:47,637
and pretend the misery
doesn't exist.

467
00:20:47,724 --> 00:20:48,769
[knocking]

468
00:20:48,856 --> 00:20:50,553
Boss, you might wanna see this.

469
00:20:54,078 --> 00:20:55,776
[Cho]
This is from a security camera
across the street.

470
00:20:55,863 --> 00:20:57,995
It was the third incident
in two weeks.

471
00:20:58,082 --> 00:21:00,171
Building owner said Hodge didn't
wanna report the earlier ones

472
00:21:00,259 --> 00:21:02,086
'because he didn't want
Deerfield PD combing through'

473
00:21:02,173 --> 00:21:03,784
his office and accidentally
finding something

474
00:21:03,871 --> 00:21:05,220
in his Sinner Saints file.

475
00:21:05,307 --> 00:21:06,961
There.

476
00:21:07,048 --> 00:21:08,223
Magnify.

477
00:21:10,660 --> 00:21:11,879
'The woman
from the parking lot?'

478
00:21:13,968 --> 00:21:15,970
She certainly gets around.

479
00:21:16,057 --> 00:21:18,277
[instrumental music]

480
00:21:22,193 --> 00:21:23,891
[indistinct chatter]

481
00:21:23,978 --> 00:21:25,893
[McBride]
'Chaos Brigade
controls distribution'

482
00:21:25,980 --> 00:21:28,461
over in Rancho Rosa,
but I figure if we move

483
00:21:28,548 --> 00:21:30,158
'right now, we can
move into Stratton--'

484
00:21:30,245 --> 00:21:31,681
What's up, my brothers?

485
00:21:31,768 --> 00:21:32,943
[clears throat]

486
00:21:35,206 --> 00:21:37,383
We just have one quick
follow-up question for you.

487
00:21:39,646 --> 00:21:43,389
I've exceeded my quota
of answering cops' questions.

488
00:21:43,476 --> 00:21:44,694
And my quota of crazy.

489
00:21:46,522 --> 00:21:48,176
The woman,
in the parking lot.

490
00:21:50,918 --> 00:21:52,441
Uh, like I said,
she must have mistaken me--

491
00:21:52,528 --> 00:21:54,835
She was seen vandalizing
Hodge's office.

492
00:21:58,839 --> 00:22:00,710
She find anything
she shouldn't have?

493
00:22:00,797 --> 00:22:04,061
His files were intact.
She got nothing.

494
00:22:04,148 --> 00:22:05,933
We have nothing further
to talk about, then.

495
00:22:06,020 --> 00:22:08,762
The sooner this case is closed,
the sooner we're gone

496
00:22:08,849 --> 00:22:10,677
and you're back
to business as usual.

497
00:22:10,764 --> 00:22:13,157
[instrumental music]

498
00:22:18,206 --> 00:22:20,556
Last name is Guthrie.

499
00:22:20,643 --> 00:22:24,647
She's the sister of a gentleman
I was accused of killing.

500
00:22:24,734 --> 00:22:26,519
Falsely, of course.

501
00:22:26,606 --> 00:22:28,216
'Trial was a couple
of weeks ago.'

502
00:22:29,783 --> 00:22:32,438
Gordon hit a home run.
Got me off.

503
00:22:32,525 --> 00:22:33,961
And you weren't eager
to ID her

504
00:22:34,048 --> 00:22:36,137
because you didn't want us
poking around your case?

505
00:22:36,224 --> 00:22:38,531
Hey, all I know is
that she's been coming around

506
00:22:38,618 --> 00:22:42,273
from time to time, saying
some very offensive things.

507
00:22:43,884 --> 00:22:45,102
Thanks for your cooperation.

508
00:22:46,756 --> 00:22:48,192
You think she killed Gordon?

509
00:22:49,585 --> 00:22:52,414
Like I said,
thanks for your cooperation.

510
00:22:54,329 --> 00:22:56,679
I've got one last question.

511
00:22:56,766 --> 00:22:59,813
If Hodge wasn't the informant
in your gang..

512
00:22:59,900 --> 00:23:01,075
...who do you think it is?

513
00:23:01,162 --> 00:23:02,555
I mean,
I tried asking the DA

514
00:23:02,642 --> 00:23:04,383
but he's kind of
a secretive bastard, huh?

515
00:23:05,993 --> 00:23:07,124
What do you think?

516
00:23:09,300 --> 00:23:11,738
Mr. Jane,
we're a motorcycle club.

517
00:23:11,825 --> 00:23:13,740
Not a gang.

518
00:23:13,827 --> 00:23:16,699
And I can assure you
there is no informant.

519
00:23:16,786 --> 00:23:18,962
Well, you'd know best.

520
00:23:26,013 --> 00:23:27,754
Why does he keep going on
about this informant?

521
00:23:29,538 --> 00:23:31,627
He's just talking.

522
00:23:31,714 --> 00:23:33,499
Let's get down to business.

523
00:23:36,893 --> 00:23:38,329
So, Miss Guthrie?

524
00:23:38,417 --> 00:23:41,724
Von McBride should be
sitting here, not me.

525
00:23:41,811 --> 00:23:43,944
Court docs say your brother,
Rick was an auto mechanic.

526
00:23:44,031 --> 00:23:45,989
McBride blamed him
for screwing up a repair

527
00:23:46,076 --> 00:23:47,861
and your brother
refused to redo it.

528
00:23:47,948 --> 00:23:49,689
McBride allegedly got angry
and killed him.

529
00:23:49,776 --> 00:23:52,213
Not allegedly.
He killed him.

530
00:23:53,997 --> 00:23:56,347
He beat him to death
with a crowbar.

531
00:23:56,435 --> 00:23:58,437
- He murdered him.
- And the jury disagreed.

532
00:24:00,003 --> 00:24:02,049
McBride acted
in self-defense, right?

533
00:24:02,136 --> 00:24:03,659
That's because
that lawyer, Hodge

534
00:24:03,746 --> 00:24:06,488
made it look like
it was my brother's fault.

535
00:24:06,575 --> 00:24:08,969
He started throwing around
all these lies about my brother.

536
00:24:09,056 --> 00:24:11,058
Saying that my brother
was a druggie.

537
00:24:11,145 --> 00:24:14,235
That he was aggressive.
That he was mentally unstable.

538
00:24:14,322 --> 00:24:16,498
So you get all worked up,
harass the gang

539
00:24:16,585 --> 00:24:17,804
trash Hodge's office,
right?

540
00:24:19,196 --> 00:24:21,808
You wanna arrest me
for that. Go ahead.

541
00:24:21,895 --> 00:24:23,810
I'm not gonna fight you.
I'm too tired.

542
00:24:23,897 --> 00:24:25,115
You ever try Hodge's home?

543
00:24:26,247 --> 00:24:27,683
Once.

544
00:24:27,770 --> 00:24:28,945
But his kid came outside.

545
00:24:30,077 --> 00:24:32,079
I don't have a beef with him.

546
00:24:32,166 --> 00:24:34,211
So I took off
before I could do anything.

547
00:24:34,298 --> 00:24:35,778
And what were you gonna do?

548
00:24:35,865 --> 00:24:36,953
I don't know.

549
00:24:37,040 --> 00:24:38,215
I was..

550
00:24:41,392 --> 00:24:42,524
I don't know.

551
00:24:44,613 --> 00:24:46,354
I wanted Hodge
to understand

552
00:24:46,441 --> 00:24:48,530
what he had done to me
and to my family.

553
00:24:48,617 --> 00:24:50,010
And when was this?

554
00:24:52,447 --> 00:24:54,754
- Two days ago.
- The day of the murder.

555
00:24:54,841 --> 00:24:56,582
- Where were you that night?
- Home.

556
00:24:56,669 --> 00:24:58,061
Can anyone verify it?

557
00:24:58,148 --> 00:25:00,107
I live alone,
but I didn't--

558
00:25:00,194 --> 00:25:01,412
Now, six months ago

559
00:25:01,500 --> 00:25:03,937
you were arrested
in a road rage incident.

560
00:25:04,024 --> 00:25:05,634
Got out of your car
at a red light.

561
00:25:05,721 --> 00:25:07,201
Attacked a man
in an SUV.

562
00:25:07,288 --> 00:25:08,942
What does this have
to do with anything?

563
00:25:09,029 --> 00:25:11,292
You're an angry person
and you express it physically.

564
00:25:13,250 --> 00:25:16,036
I'm not angry.
I am sad.

565
00:25:16,123 --> 00:25:18,038
My brother was a good man.

566
00:25:21,781 --> 00:25:23,043
The only crime he committed

567
00:25:23,130 --> 00:25:25,349
was standing up
to that bastard, McBride.

568
00:25:25,436 --> 00:25:27,264
Hodge blackens the name
of your dead brother

569
00:25:27,351 --> 00:25:29,049
and gets Von McBride off.

570
00:25:29,136 --> 00:25:30,441
'Now maybe trashing his office'

571
00:25:30,529 --> 00:25:32,008
'didn't give you
enough satisfaction.'

572
00:25:32,095 --> 00:25:34,576
Perfectly understandable
if your frustration boils over.

573
00:25:34,663 --> 00:25:35,751
And you can't touch Von McBride.

574
00:25:35,838 --> 00:25:36,796
He's got 20 bikers around him

575
00:25:36,883 --> 00:25:38,362
all the time.

576
00:25:38,449 --> 00:25:39,712
So maybe you go
for the easier target.

577
00:25:41,975 --> 00:25:44,107
I didn't kill Gordon Hodge.

578
00:25:44,194 --> 00:25:46,588
But I'm sure as hell
glad that he's dead.

579
00:25:49,852 --> 00:25:51,332
[Cho]
She'd been to his house
that day.

580
00:25:51,419 --> 00:25:53,639
Could have laid in wait
and followed him later.

581
00:25:53,726 --> 00:25:55,641
Plus, she was out for revenge,
no more powerful motive.

582
00:25:55,728 --> 00:25:57,773
We don't have nearly enough
to charge her.

583
00:25:57,860 --> 00:25:59,601
I say we hold her
on the vandalism.

584
00:25:59,688 --> 00:26:01,734
Try to dig up something that
puts her at the murder scene.

585
00:26:01,821 --> 00:26:04,258
Or you could release her.

586
00:26:04,345 --> 00:26:06,303
She's obviously impulsive
and sloppy enough

587
00:26:06,390 --> 00:26:08,349
'to get caught on camera.'

588
00:26:08,436 --> 00:26:10,612
She'll think
she's bought herself some time.

589
00:26:10,699 --> 00:26:12,353
And she'd try something
to cover her tracks

590
00:26:12,440 --> 00:26:13,615
and implicate herself.

591
00:26:16,444 --> 00:26:18,272
Cut her loose,
then let's shadow her.

592
00:26:18,359 --> 00:26:19,534
Yes, boss.

593
00:26:20,970 --> 00:26:22,145
[sighs]

594
00:26:22,232 --> 00:26:24,234
Where are you going?

595
00:26:24,321 --> 00:26:26,323
Fresh air.

596
00:26:26,410 --> 00:26:27,586
All this murder talk..

597
00:26:27,673 --> 00:26:30,893
"...is rank.
It stinks to heaven.

598
00:26:30,980 --> 00:26:33,722
It hath the primal
eldest curse upon 't."

599
00:26:35,332 --> 00:26:36,507
Shakespeare.

600
00:26:38,814 --> 00:26:41,469
[instrumental music]

601
00:26:55,526 --> 00:26:57,920
[tires screeching]

602
00:27:00,662 --> 00:27:02,185
Little less pressure
on the brake pedal.

603
00:27:03,839 --> 00:27:05,449
Is your mom here?

604
00:27:05,536 --> 00:27:07,887
Market. That's why
I'm confined to the driveway.

605
00:27:07,974 --> 00:27:09,192
Ah!

606
00:27:09,279 --> 00:27:11,194
You want me
to have her call you?

607
00:27:11,281 --> 00:27:13,719
We know Felicia Guthrie
trespassed on the property

608
00:27:13,806 --> 00:27:15,068
the day your dad was killed.

609
00:27:15,155 --> 00:27:17,897
I-I just need to hear
what happened.

610
00:27:17,984 --> 00:27:20,813
Uh, I was leaving for school.

611
00:27:20,900 --> 00:27:22,771
I saw her hop the gate and come
running up the driveway.

612
00:27:22,858 --> 00:27:24,991
So I ran out
to try to stop her.

613
00:27:25,078 --> 00:27:27,167
And she was yelling
all this stuff about my dad

614
00:27:27,254 --> 00:27:30,605
lying about her brother
and getting Von McBride off.

615
00:27:30,692 --> 00:27:33,608
- Then she just ran away.
- Did your parents see her?

616
00:27:33,695 --> 00:27:36,698
No. Dad was already at work,
and mom was in the shower.

617
00:27:36,785 --> 00:27:39,353
Huh. Any reason you didn't
bring this up earlier?

618
00:27:41,094 --> 00:27:43,792
I don't know. I felt
bad for her, I guess.

619
00:27:43,879 --> 00:27:45,489
Didn't want her
to get in trouble.

620
00:27:45,576 --> 00:27:48,710
Well, just needed
to confirm. Thanks.

621
00:27:48,797 --> 00:27:50,625
[engine grinds]

622
00:27:50,712 --> 00:27:51,844
Whoa!

623
00:27:51,931 --> 00:27:53,236
God!

624
00:27:53,323 --> 00:27:55,238
You need to relax.

625
00:27:55,325 --> 00:27:57,588
It's not gonna help. I'm never
gonna get the hang of this.

626
00:27:57,676 --> 00:28:00,200
That's an easy fix.
You need the right instructor.

627
00:28:00,287 --> 00:28:02,245
Alright, so now you can
speed up a little.

628
00:28:04,552 --> 00:28:07,294
'Excellent. I like how
you're keeping your distance.'

629
00:28:07,381 --> 00:28:09,252
Just trust your instincts.
They're always right.

630
00:28:11,124 --> 00:28:12,647
You're a good instructor.

631
00:28:12,734 --> 00:28:14,997
Yeah, I am,
probably because I have

632
00:28:15,084 --> 00:28:18,174
zero emotional investment
in how you do.

633
00:28:18,261 --> 00:28:20,046
Unlike your father
who I'm guessing

634
00:28:20,133 --> 00:28:22,265
got annoyed
with every mistake you made.

635
00:28:22,352 --> 00:28:24,180
He wasn't the most patient guy.

636
00:28:24,267 --> 00:28:26,313
Probably didn't help that
he was always on his cell phone.

637
00:28:28,097 --> 00:28:29,969
I've been living with his job
my whole life.

638
00:28:30,056 --> 00:28:31,187
You get used to it.

639
00:28:33,450 --> 00:28:34,843
You also get used to the drugs

640
00:28:34,930 --> 00:28:36,279
and the cheating
on your mother?

641
00:28:38,107 --> 00:28:39,543
He promised he'd stop.

642
00:28:39,630 --> 00:28:41,458
Yeah.

643
00:28:41,545 --> 00:28:43,156
Can't be easy
going through life

644
00:28:43,243 --> 00:28:45,680
being labeled
the gang lawyer's son.

645
00:28:45,767 --> 00:28:47,247
It wasn't really that bad.

646
00:28:47,334 --> 00:28:49,249
I mean, girls would come
up to me all the time.

647
00:28:49,336 --> 00:28:52,208
Talk to me about dad
and the gang, like I'm cool.

648
00:28:52,295 --> 00:28:55,211
Instead of a geek,
which I basically am.

649
00:28:55,298 --> 00:28:56,430
Everybody is.

650
00:28:58,780 --> 00:28:59,912
I am.

651
00:29:02,305 --> 00:29:05,482
If he was my father,
I tell ya, I-I..

652
00:29:05,569 --> 00:29:06,875
...I'd be mad at him.

653
00:29:08,572 --> 00:29:10,226
Dad didn't mean
to hurt anyone.

654
00:29:10,313 --> 00:29:13,186
- He was just doing his job.
- Right.

655
00:29:13,273 --> 00:29:16,667
Well, I guess I'd still
love him if he was my father.

656
00:29:16,755 --> 00:29:18,365
Can't say I'd cut him
the same kind of slack

657
00:29:18,452 --> 00:29:20,628
if I was married to him.

658
00:29:20,715 --> 00:29:22,978
Are you trying
to blame my mom?

659
00:29:23,065 --> 00:29:26,329
- 'Cause if you are..
- What?

660
00:29:26,416 --> 00:29:27,983
You're wrong, that's all.

661
00:29:28,070 --> 00:29:30,507
She loved him too.

662
00:29:30,594 --> 00:29:32,553
Well, that brings us
back to Felicia Guthrie

663
00:29:32,640 --> 00:29:33,554
who didn't love him at all.

664
00:29:33,641 --> 00:29:34,729
What exactly did she say

665
00:29:34,816 --> 00:29:36,252
to you when you saw her?

666
00:29:36,339 --> 00:29:37,601
It was hard to tell.

667
00:29:37,688 --> 00:29:40,039
She was just, you know,
ranting, basically.

668
00:29:41,301 --> 00:29:42,476
Didn't make much sense.

669
00:29:54,967 --> 00:29:57,143
Very nicely done.

670
00:29:57,230 --> 00:30:00,363
You'll be out cruising
on Saturday nights in no time.

671
00:30:00,450 --> 00:30:03,192
Just remember,
trust your instincts.

672
00:30:03,279 --> 00:30:04,367
They're always right.

673
00:30:04,454 --> 00:30:05,804
Thank you.

674
00:30:05,891 --> 00:30:06,935
And thanks for
the driving lesson.

675
00:30:07,022 --> 00:30:08,154
Yeah.

676
00:30:10,721 --> 00:30:13,115
[dogs barking]

677
00:30:14,464 --> 00:30:16,075
Still no movement.

678
00:30:16,162 --> 00:30:17,990
Looks like Miss Guthrie's
in for the night.

679
00:30:21,384 --> 00:30:22,690
Talk to Van Pelt recently?

680
00:30:22,777 --> 00:30:23,909
Yep.

681
00:30:25,867 --> 00:30:27,086
- Any progress?
- Nope.

682
00:30:29,566 --> 00:30:30,567
[engine rumbling in distance]

683
00:30:30,654 --> 00:30:32,918
You hear that?

684
00:30:33,005 --> 00:30:34,484
Yeah.

685
00:30:34,571 --> 00:30:36,965
[dramatic music]

686
00:30:46,888 --> 00:30:48,107
They're gonna go
after Felicia.

687
00:30:49,891 --> 00:30:51,284
McBride thinks
she killed Hodge.

688
00:30:51,371 --> 00:30:52,676
He wants payback.

689
00:30:52,763 --> 00:30:54,635
Officers on Hampton,
North of Lexington

690
00:30:54,722 --> 00:30:56,115
request
immediate assistance.

691
00:30:58,117 --> 00:31:00,510
[music continues]

692
00:31:04,123 --> 00:31:05,820
What the hell's going on?

693
00:31:05,907 --> 00:31:07,691
Go back in your house
and stay down.

694
00:31:10,564 --> 00:31:12,871
[music continues]

695
00:31:28,234 --> 00:31:32,064
Do the smart thing
and get out of here right now.

696
00:31:32,151 --> 00:31:34,240
We're not doing
anything illegal.

697
00:31:34,327 --> 00:31:36,198
Disorderly conduct

698
00:31:36,285 --> 00:31:39,723
concealed weapons,
blown exhaust pipes

699
00:31:39,810 --> 00:31:43,379
probably a couple of
outstanding warrants in there.

700
00:31:43,466 --> 00:31:46,643
- 'Screw you, pig!'
- 'No, screw you!'

701
00:31:46,730 --> 00:31:48,863
We could bust
half you clowns right now.

702
00:31:52,301 --> 00:31:53,737
So what's it gonna be?

703
00:31:54,913 --> 00:31:57,306
[music continues]

704
00:32:04,270 --> 00:32:05,619
We'll be seeing you around.

705
00:32:12,626 --> 00:32:14,584
[engines revving]

706
00:32:14,671 --> 00:32:16,369
[indistinct yelling]

707
00:32:18,501 --> 00:32:20,416
Scumbag!

708
00:32:20,503 --> 00:32:21,896
[laughing]

709
00:32:28,250 --> 00:32:29,469
You really don't like bikers.

710
00:32:38,826 --> 00:32:41,481
[Felicia]
'If they think they can
intimidate me, they're wrong.'

711
00:32:41,568 --> 00:32:43,874
Felicia, temperatures
are running hot

712
00:32:43,962 --> 00:32:46,529
so I need you to stay away
from the gang's bar from now on.

713
00:32:46,616 --> 00:32:49,576
[Felicia]
'Yeah. I'll stay away
when you arrest Von McBride.'

714
00:32:49,663 --> 00:32:51,273
And what were you people
doing out here, anyway?

715
00:32:51,360 --> 00:32:53,406
Oh, we think you killed,
uh, Gordon Hodge

716
00:32:53,493 --> 00:32:56,887
so Agent Cho and Rigsby
have been watching you.

717
00:32:59,281 --> 00:33:01,370
Oh, come on,
she was never gonna buy

718
00:33:01,457 --> 00:33:03,677
"We just happened to be
in the neighborhood."

719
00:33:03,764 --> 00:33:06,375
I told you I had nothing
to do with that.

720
00:33:06,462 --> 00:33:08,595
And who told you
that you could go in my house?

721
00:33:08,682 --> 00:33:11,467
Oh, this? I just needed
some tea. Cut through the chill.

722
00:33:11,554 --> 00:33:14,209
Chill, my ass.
You were looking for evidence.

723
00:33:14,296 --> 00:33:16,777
- Felicia, take it easy.
- Don't tell me to take it easy.

724
00:33:16,864 --> 00:33:18,953
When this guy's rifling
through my underwear drawer

725
00:33:19,040 --> 00:33:20,650
looking for a weapon.

726
00:33:20,737 --> 00:33:21,956
It was your closet, actually,
I was looking

727
00:33:22,043 --> 00:33:24,002
for blood-splattered shoes.

728
00:33:24,089 --> 00:33:25,916
- Get off my property.
- You're very touchy.

729
00:33:26,004 --> 00:33:27,135
Go.

730
00:33:31,879 --> 00:33:33,011
You really looked
through her closet?

731
00:33:33,098 --> 00:33:34,186
Laundry, too.

732
00:33:34,273 --> 00:33:35,274
She's been angry and emotional

733
00:33:35,361 --> 00:33:37,319
about her brother.

734
00:33:37,406 --> 00:33:38,929
Which means
that she was sloppy

735
00:33:39,017 --> 00:33:40,583
about Hodge's murder.

736
00:33:40,670 --> 00:33:42,237
Dragged evidence
home with her.

737
00:33:42,324 --> 00:33:43,847
It's just not inside.

738
00:33:43,934 --> 00:33:45,501
Well, there's no garage
or toolshed.

739
00:33:45,588 --> 00:33:47,242
Well, I looked everywhere.

740
00:33:47,329 --> 00:33:49,810
Well, everywhere
except the...garbage.

741
00:33:49,897 --> 00:33:51,812
Why not?

742
00:33:51,899 --> 00:33:53,074
Well, it's garbage.

743
00:33:54,597 --> 00:33:56,382
- Are you done with that?
- Almost.

744
00:34:02,431 --> 00:34:04,651
Yes, the case
is still ongoing

745
00:34:04,738 --> 00:34:06,740
and you are
a person of interest.

746
00:34:06,827 --> 00:34:08,394
'I'd advise you
not to leave town.'

747
00:34:10,352 --> 00:34:11,397
Boss?

748
00:34:11,484 --> 00:34:12,615
Excuse me.

749
00:34:14,965 --> 00:34:16,010
Do you see that?

750
00:34:18,230 --> 00:34:19,318
What's goin' on?

751
00:34:19,405 --> 00:34:20,797
Stay there. Don't move.

752
00:34:25,150 --> 00:34:26,934
[Rigsby]
It's the victim's
missing cufflink.

753
00:34:32,244 --> 00:34:33,767
I didn't do anything wrong.

754
00:34:33,854 --> 00:34:35,638
McBride must have set me up.

755
00:34:35,725 --> 00:34:37,205
Rigsby, put her
in interview one.

756
00:34:37,292 --> 00:34:39,251
Boss, Nina and Lucas Hodge
are here to see you.

757
00:34:39,338 --> 00:34:41,122
- Did she say why?
- 'Cause I asked them down here.

758
00:34:41,209 --> 00:34:42,776
Rigsby, could you bring her
through here, please?

759
00:34:42,863 --> 00:34:44,082
It will just take a minute.

760
00:34:45,474 --> 00:34:46,867
Thank you.

761
00:34:46,954 --> 00:34:48,303
Are you gonna tell me
what this is about?

762
00:34:48,390 --> 00:34:49,696
I'm just closing
your case.

763
00:34:53,395 --> 00:34:55,484
Thanks for coming down,
Mrs. Hodge.

764
00:34:55,571 --> 00:34:58,183
This woman's name
is Felicia Guthrie.

765
00:34:58,270 --> 00:35:00,315
She murdered your husband
out of revenge for getting

766
00:35:00,402 --> 00:35:02,839
Von McBride off a charge
for killing her brother.

767
00:35:02,926 --> 00:35:04,754
- Oh, my God!
- No, I did not kill anyone--

768
00:35:04,841 --> 00:35:06,365
Uh, we have evidence.

769
00:35:09,194 --> 00:35:10,543
We just need
your permission for, uh..

770
00:35:10,630 --> 00:35:12,371
...Lucas to make a formal
statement, saying that

771
00:35:12,458 --> 00:35:14,460
he saw her at your house
the day of the murder.

772
00:35:14,547 --> 00:35:16,810
- You saw her?
- He can fill you in later.

773
00:35:16,897 --> 00:35:19,682
His statement will give us
a better chance at a conviction.

774
00:35:19,769 --> 00:35:22,468
- Absolutely. Anything you need.
- Great. Thank you.

775
00:35:22,555 --> 00:35:25,993
Lucas, if you can confirm
that this is who you saw

776
00:35:26,080 --> 00:35:27,255
then you'll be on your way.

777
00:35:29,170 --> 00:35:30,737
What's gonna happen to her?

778
00:35:30,824 --> 00:35:32,608
Well, probably life in prison.

779
00:35:32,695 --> 00:35:35,742
Uh, if she's lucky, she might
get paroled in 25 years.

780
00:35:35,829 --> 00:35:38,614
No! I swear, I didn't..

781
00:35:38,701 --> 00:35:40,312
- I didn't touch him--
- 'Shut up!'

782
00:35:40,399 --> 00:35:42,009
You took everything from us.

783
00:35:42,096 --> 00:35:44,968
Lucas, we need to book her now,
so could you identify her?

784
00:35:45,055 --> 00:35:47,406
No, she wasn't the one.

785
00:35:47,493 --> 00:35:48,581
I mean, yeah,
she came to the house--

786
00:35:48,668 --> 00:35:50,278
Great. Thanks.
That's all we need.

787
00:35:50,365 --> 00:35:51,932
- Take her away, guys.
- 'No, I didn't do anything.'

788
00:35:52,019 --> 00:35:53,412
- Thank you.
- 'I didn't do anything wrong.'

789
00:35:53,499 --> 00:35:55,370
Trust your instincts, Lucas.
They're always right.

790
00:35:55,457 --> 00:35:56,676
[Felicia]
'I'm telling the truth!'

791
00:35:57,720 --> 00:35:59,896
Let's go.

792
00:35:59,983 --> 00:36:02,290
- She couldn't have done it.
- What makes you say that?

793
00:36:02,377 --> 00:36:03,944
- I just know.
- 'Lucas, they have evidence.'

794
00:36:04,031 --> 00:36:05,946
- This bitch killed your--
- Don't call her that.

795
00:36:06,033 --> 00:36:07,861
It wasn't her.

796
00:36:07,948 --> 00:36:09,210
The only way we can know

797
00:36:09,297 --> 00:36:10,994
for certain is if
you tell us who did it.

798
00:36:11,081 --> 00:36:12,866
Okay, stop talking to my son.

799
00:36:12,953 --> 00:36:14,911
You've got your statement.
Lucas, let's go.

800
00:36:14,998 --> 00:36:16,522
- 'Come on. Let's go.'
- No.

801
00:36:16,609 --> 00:36:18,045
- Lucas--
- Stop.

802
00:36:26,880 --> 00:36:28,055
It was me.

803
00:36:30,666 --> 00:36:32,146
We were out
for a driving lesson.

804
00:36:33,756 --> 00:36:36,542
I was driving badly
that night.

805
00:36:36,629 --> 00:36:38,239
My dad was on the phone
the whole time

806
00:36:38,326 --> 00:36:40,937
like he always was.

807
00:36:41,024 --> 00:36:43,505
He'd get mad every time
I'd make a mistake but..

808
00:36:43,592 --> 00:36:45,377
...I just couldn't seem
to concentrate.

809
00:36:45,464 --> 00:36:47,292
Because of your run-in
with Felicia Guthrie that day?

810
00:36:49,424 --> 00:36:51,731
You didn't talk about her
until I asked

811
00:36:51,818 --> 00:36:53,994
'cause you felt sorry for her.

812
00:36:54,081 --> 00:36:56,431
You didn't wanna draw
suspicion to her

813
00:36:56,518 --> 00:36:58,259
because you knew
she didn't do it.

814
00:37:00,000 --> 00:37:02,045
You were trying to do
the right thing.

815
00:37:02,132 --> 00:37:04,570
I just kept seeing her
in the driveway.

816
00:37:04,657 --> 00:37:08,704
Crying, yelling about how
my dad lied about her brother.

817
00:37:10,228 --> 00:37:12,099
His phone just kept ringing.

818
00:37:12,186 --> 00:37:14,928
And he'd get mad at me
and I'd screw up worse.

819
00:37:15,015 --> 00:37:16,625
And I just..

820
00:37:16,712 --> 00:37:18,801
I couldn't take it anymore.

821
00:37:18,888 --> 00:37:20,716
Next time, his phone rang..

822
00:37:20,803 --> 00:37:23,589
...I grabbed it from him.
I heard her voice.

823
00:37:23,676 --> 00:37:27,941
[Constance]
Hey, Gordon, baby,
it's me. Can you talk?

824
00:37:28,028 --> 00:37:30,987
That biker bitch,
Diamond.

825
00:37:31,074 --> 00:37:32,511
'She kept calling him
Gordon, baby.'

826
00:37:32,598 --> 00:37:34,687
'Said she really
wanted to see him.'

827
00:37:34,774 --> 00:37:37,646
Felicia Guthrie was right.
He was a liar.

828
00:37:41,781 --> 00:37:43,609
I threw the phone into the
woods, and he got really mad.

829
00:37:45,263 --> 00:37:48,004
He promised me he'd stop.

830
00:37:48,091 --> 00:37:49,789
Doing drugs
and cheating on my mom.

831
00:37:51,443 --> 00:37:53,140
Like an idiot,
I believed him.

832
00:37:53,967 --> 00:37:55,490
[grunting]

833
00:38:04,847 --> 00:38:06,675
I called my mom.

834
00:38:06,762 --> 00:38:08,721
She told me what to do.

835
00:38:08,808 --> 00:38:10,853
'I took all the stuff
to make it look like a robbery'

836
00:38:10,940 --> 00:38:12,899
but I couldn't get
that damn cufflink out.

837
00:38:14,640 --> 00:38:16,859
'So I ditched his car
in the lake.'

838
00:38:16,946 --> 00:38:18,470
She drove me home.

839
00:38:18,557 --> 00:38:20,167
The lie gets heavy fast,
doesn't it?

840
00:38:23,126 --> 00:38:24,432
I expect after a while

841
00:38:24,519 --> 00:38:25,651
you wanted to go to the police

842
00:38:25,738 --> 00:38:26,869
and tell them the truth.

843
00:38:28,131 --> 00:38:29,742
Sometimes I wanted to.

844
00:38:29,829 --> 00:38:31,047
Mom said no.

845
00:38:32,875 --> 00:38:34,355
She promised
it would be okay.

846
00:38:36,096 --> 00:38:37,880
Well, it might be..

847
00:38:37,967 --> 00:38:39,142
...someday.

848
00:38:44,322 --> 00:38:45,453
Let's go.

849
00:38:47,890 --> 00:38:49,414
Put your hand out.

850
00:38:54,984 --> 00:38:56,682
I'm sorry, mom.

851
00:38:56,769 --> 00:38:58,771
[Van Pelt]
'Mrs. Hodge,
we need to talk now.'

852
00:39:02,427 --> 00:39:03,558
[instrumental music]

853
00:39:05,604 --> 00:39:08,650
You know, I have to wonder
how that cufflink Rigsby found

854
00:39:08,737 --> 00:39:10,652
made its way
to Felicia Guthrie's house.

855
00:39:10,739 --> 00:39:11,827
That is a conundrum.

856
00:39:11,914 --> 00:39:13,438
Because I'll bet
a year's salary

857
00:39:13,525 --> 00:39:15,527
that if I look
in the evidence locker

858
00:39:15,614 --> 00:39:18,573
the cufflink we found on Hodge
will have mysteriously vanished.

859
00:39:20,575 --> 00:39:22,751
Okay.

860
00:39:22,838 --> 00:39:24,884
I needed Lucas to see
Felicia get arrested.

861
00:39:24,971 --> 00:39:27,147
You needed hard evidence
to charge Felicia.

862
00:39:27,234 --> 00:39:28,366
So..

863
00:39:30,411 --> 00:39:31,760
...I made it happen.

864
00:39:31,847 --> 00:39:33,109
By making
an innocent woman think

865
00:39:33,196 --> 00:39:34,850
she was gonna go
to prison?

866
00:39:34,937 --> 00:39:36,852
As if her life wasn't
hard enough already.

867
00:39:36,939 --> 00:39:40,029
Yes, you're right.
She doesdeserve some justice.

868
00:39:40,116 --> 00:39:42,118
It's good to see
you care.

869
00:39:42,205 --> 00:39:44,904
You know, sarcasm
is the lowest form of wit?

870
00:39:50,518 --> 00:39:53,173
[heavy metal music]

871
00:39:53,260 --> 00:39:55,480
...next Tuesday,
we need about..

872
00:39:55,567 --> 00:39:56,829
...about six, ten bikes.

873
00:39:56,916 --> 00:39:58,657
- So be here--
- Yeah.

874
00:39:58,744 --> 00:40:00,485
[phone ringing]
This will be our real gig.
Hold on.

875
00:40:05,620 --> 00:40:06,752
Yeah?

876
00:40:10,973 --> 00:40:12,366
Alright.

877
00:40:12,453 --> 00:40:13,411
I'll be back in a minute.

878
00:40:22,985 --> 00:40:24,987
[Jane]
'Hey, psst.'

879
00:40:26,119 --> 00:40:27,294
'Over here.'

880
00:40:39,088 --> 00:40:40,307
What's up?

881
00:40:42,309 --> 00:40:43,528
Uh, I just thought
you might wanna know

882
00:40:43,615 --> 00:40:45,007
we caught
Gordon Hodge's killer.

883
00:40:46,095 --> 00:40:48,010
It was his son.

884
00:40:48,097 --> 00:40:49,925
Lot of issues between 'em.

885
00:40:50,012 --> 00:40:53,146
And you felt the need to tell
me this from the shadows

886
00:40:53,233 --> 00:40:54,626
dressed in this get-up?

887
00:40:54,713 --> 00:40:56,845
Self-preservation.

888
00:40:56,932 --> 00:40:59,239
I figured I've worn out
my welcome with your friends.

889
00:41:00,196 --> 00:41:01,763
That's it?

890
00:41:01,850 --> 00:41:02,982
This is what
you had to tell me?

891
00:41:03,069 --> 00:41:06,333
Well, no.
There's, uh, another reason.

892
00:41:09,728 --> 00:41:10,990
You open that envelope..

893
00:41:12,513 --> 00:41:14,776
...and the rat in your gang
will be revealed.

894
00:41:14,863 --> 00:41:17,126
Oh, the rat.

895
00:41:17,213 --> 00:41:19,825
[door opening]

896
00:41:19,912 --> 00:41:21,783
Now turn around and try
not to look too guilty.

897
00:41:28,311 --> 00:41:29,748
What was that about?

898
00:41:29,835 --> 00:41:31,532
What, this?
This is, uh..

899
00:41:31,619 --> 00:41:34,100
[chuckles]
It's kind of funny,
actually.

900
00:41:34,187 --> 00:41:35,275
Funny?

901
00:41:35,362 --> 00:41:37,059
[dramatic music]

902
00:41:39,105 --> 00:41:40,410
Selling us out is funny?

903
00:41:42,021 --> 00:41:44,371
- Hey! Hey!
- Come on, get him inside.

904
00:41:44,458 --> 00:41:47,287
[McBride]
'Hey! Let go, man!'

905
00:41:47,374 --> 00:41:49,768
[instrumental music]

906
00:41:51,334 --> 00:41:52,640
I was set up!

907
00:41:56,775 --> 00:41:59,168
[music continues]

908
00:42:10,615 --> 00:42:12,878
[Jane]
Stay tuned for scenes
from our next episode.

909
00:42:16,229 --> 00:42:17,491
[theme music]

